## Tri-Modal Molecular Driver Recovery and Multi-View Fingerprints

The linear entrypoint maps the 500 multi-omic features directly onto the low-dimensional latent coordinates, while `pysimlr.loading_inference` refits the full pipeline across 100 half-sample splits and 20 cross-view permutations to separate reproducible drivers from in-sample selection noise. @fig-brca-trimodal-waterfall displays `pysimlr.plot_top_features` on the ER-aligned component learned by `LEND` across the three molecular modalities (`brca_er_loadings.json` from `scripts/paper_brca_loadings.py`), @fig-brca-feature-chord maps the stability-selected and interval-significant biomarkers across all three views onto components `C1–C3` via `pysimlr.plot_feature_chord`, and @fig-brca-view-radar summarizes each assay's training and held-out coupling, held-out reconstruction $R^2$, normalized effective rank, and sparsity via `pysimlr.plot_view_radar`.

